                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1cb39804-fec0-3e50-9992-320aa97dce97",
                        "entry_id": "56c5006e-04b7-3380-b762-4f3debc6d775",
                        "glosses": [
                            "прост. прихрамывать, ковылять, идти, хромая"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "07bf6833-22ef-49e4-bf44-9f9ee4cd45f4",
                                "sense_id": "1cb39804-fec0-3e50-9992-320aa97dce97",
                                "text": "Восковые, с чёрно-провалившимися ямами вместо глаз, в рваном вонючем белье, они тащились, ползли, шкандыбали, и все в одном направлении ― к шоссе."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b96b8e31-2a9d-4a3b-a9ce-e22cf35e0ecc",
                                "sense_id": "1cb39804-fec0-3e50-9992-320aa97dce97",
                                "text": "Старший из угла шкандыбает, всей пятернёй штаны на весу держит, лица на ём нет."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bbf0283f-1eba-4683-bb57-998d4f0132d3",
                                "sense_id": "1cb39804-fec0-3e50-9992-320aa97dce97",
                                "text": "Старик серчал, брёл следом за тучей, шкандыбал дырявыми хромовыми сапогами по сухим земляным глудкам."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4b9ee57d-03df-4aae-a5ca-2e416d1d469c",
                        "source_entry_id": "56c5006e-04b7-3380-b762-4f3debc6d775",
                        "source_sense_id": "1cb39804-fec0-3e50-9992-320aa97dce97",
                        "target_lang_word": "plod",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "plod",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c57aa351-e59f-33bc-b370-2e1f5d45692d",
                                        "entry_id": "1f624dd6-71cd-3eae-bdb1-cf9c8120c744",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A slow or labored walk or other motion or activity."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "87258279-bfcb-4aa6-86d0-9c763dc93946",
                                                "sense_id": "c57aa351-e59f-33bc-b370-2e1f5d45692d",
                                                "text": "We started at a brisk walk and ended at a plod."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3486550f-0ccd-40ec-89f2-b11365550401",
                                                "sense_id": "c57aa351-e59f-33bc-b370-2e1f5d45692d",
                                                "text": "Germany can’t afford to stick to the stately plod into decline that Merkel initiated any longer. Merz will have to act fast, and break things to pull the country out of the quagmire it finds itself in."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "plod",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1e57c6f2-11b2-311a-ba3d-dcc5f297a68e",
                                        "entry_id": "b2cbb123-03d2-3df3-bbfa-f37e8d3f2a22",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To walk or move slowly and heavily or laboriously (+ on, through, over)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "555ce980-6432-4df4-a9f2-4b6f57b886ea",
                                                "sense_id": "1e57c6f2-11b2-311a-ba3d-dcc5f297a68e",
                                                "text": "The beast that bears me, tired with my woe,\nPlods dully on, to bear that weight in me,"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "07da25f9-5b32-4e26-afdb-7e0c9243ecba",
                                                "sense_id": "1e57c6f2-11b2-311a-ba3d-dcc5f297a68e",
                                                "text": "I remember him as if it were yesterday, as he came plodding to the inn door, his sea chest following behind him in a handbarrow;"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "85d2e2e1-eaf5-3352-b452-dd05b43126a7",
                                        "entry_id": "b2cbb123-03d2-3df3-bbfa-f37e8d3f2a22",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To trudge over or through."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a08c114f-6457-4665-8ed2-113280ef0b1a",
                                                "sense_id": "85d2e2e1-eaf5-3352-b452-dd05b43126a7",
                                                "text": "Quest[ion]. Where was Ioseph?\nAnsw[er]. It may be, he was playing the Carpenter abrode for all their three livings, but sure it is, he was not idlely plodding the streetes, much lesse tipling in the Taverne with our idle swingers."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "193007e8-e1c0-4933-99b2-82db87b68a4b",
                                                "sense_id": "85d2e2e1-eaf5-3352-b452-dd05b43126a7",
                                                "text": "1799, Matthew Gregory Lewis, The Love of Gain, London: J. Bell, p. 50, lines 449-451,\n[…] Speed thou to Lombard-street,\nOr plod the gambling 'Change with busy feet,\n'Midst Bulls and Bears some false report to spread,"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "58577798-3a0c-4fea-9c4a-c672ab15c218",
                                                "sense_id": "85d2e2e1-eaf5-3352-b452-dd05b43126a7",
                                                "text": "Break no rosemary, bright with rime\nAnd sparkling to the cruel clime;\nNor plod the winter land to look\nFor willows in the icy brook\nTo cast them leafless round him […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "22999a47-b01e-3c44-a0b4-fc6d4cd9737a",
                                        "entry_id": "b2cbb123-03d2-3df3-bbfa-f37e8d3f2a22",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To toil; to drudge; especially, to study laboriously and patiently."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cef6b634-3f56-4db4-b283-7171d0546724",
                                                "sense_id": "22999a47-b01e-3c44-a0b4-fc6d4cd9737a",
                                                "text": "On Sundays I keep plodding along at my job."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "62979219-e51c-43ca-a848-419f47ef0ec5",
                                                "sense_id": "22999a47-b01e-3c44-a0b4-fc6d4cd9737a",
                                                "text": "1597, Michael Drayton, “Edward the fourth to Shores wife” in Englands Heroicall Epistles, London: N. Ling,\nPoore plodding schoolemen, they are farre too low,\nwhich by probations, rules and axiom’s goe,\nHe must be still familiar with the skyes,\nwhich notes the reuolutions of thine eyes;"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "01dd4fb2-8cc4-37a3-a12d-38adc4590746",
                                        "entry_id": "b2cbb123-03d2-3df3-bbfa-f37e8d3f2a22",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To extrude (soap, margarine, etc.) through a die plate so it can be cut into billets."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
